## 7. System Design & Implementation

### 7.1 Software Architecture

- **Frontend**:  
  Built with ReactJS. Pages for login, schedule management, event suggestion, and friend handling.

- **Backend**:  
  Firebase Firestore stores schedules, events, friend data  
  Firebase Auth for login  
  Firebase Hosting + Vercel for deployment  
  GitHub for version control

#### Diagram Explanation

1. **Schedule Management**: Browser → ReactJS → Firebase  
2. **Event & Friend Management**: ReactJS handles user actions → Firebase triggers real-time updates

---

### 7.2 Data Flow

- Users log in and manage time blocks, events, and friends  
- Data stored in Firebase Firestore  
- Friend requests and event proposals trigger real-time updates  
- Invitees can accept/decline and everyone sees live changes

---

### 7.3 Main Screens & Functions

- **Home**: Entry screen after login  
- **Scheduler**: Weekly planner with time blocks  
- **Event Page**: Create/edit group events  
- **Friend List**: Send/manage friend requests  
- **Customized Events**: Title, time, participants, synced to Firebase  
- **Time Blocks**: Define availability; used for group match-making

---

### 7.4 Expected Effects

- Improves group coordination with live updates  
- Quick setup of friend connections  
- Cuts down messaging clutter  
- Enables smoother group and club planning

